--- !u!114 &3671075198338702543
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 896641386104582160}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 125fb93a0146b294bb1a817431452f4a, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  ExecutableCode: "\nrotate_magic_channel(<e></e>,<e></e>);\n\n<color=#44CD8B>/*
    \nrotate_magic_channel(x, y) 0 <= x,y <= size-1  */</color>\n\n"
  HintText: Rotate the magic channels in order to connect the 2 points!
  Completed: 0
  Block: 0
  UseOutline: 1
  EnemySpawnAfterComplete: 
  Outline: {fileID: 0}
  TimeSpent: 0
  FirstTime: 0
  IgnoreTime: 0
  OirginalTile: {fileID: 859012109324736531}
  tiles: []
  tileSize: 0.15
  Side: 0
  T_Level: {fileID: 8498334479363776971}
  Level: 0
  Loading: 0
  LoadingSign: {fileID: 5581916546062173897}
  Congrats: {fileID: 6243630126143940874}
  Prompt: "You are a puzzle generator for a grid-based pipe connection game.\r\n\r\nThe
    game board is a square grid of tiles. Each tile has:\r\n- A position (`x`, `y`)\r\n-
    A type (integer 0\u20134):\r\n  - 0 = empty (no pipe)\r\n  - 1 = straight pipe
    (top-bottom)\r\n  - 2 = elbow pipe (e.g., down + right)\r\n  - 3 = T-shaped pipe
    (3 directions)\r\n  - 4 = cross pipe (all 4 directions)\r\n- A rotation: 0, 90,
    180, or 270 degrees (clockwise)\r\n\r\nYour task is to generate a **solvable
    pipe puzzle**:\r\n- Grid size is {{size}} \xD7 {{size}}\r\n- Difficulty is \"{{difficulty}}\"
    (affects complexity and distractors)\r\n- There must be **one valid pipe path**
    from a start tile to an end tile\r\n- Pipes must connect logically when rotated
    properly\r\n- The rest of the grid may contain irrelevant or misleading tiles
    depending on difficulty\r\n- All tiles must be represented in a **single array**,
    one tile per object\r\n\r\nReturn only a valid JSON object with:\r\n- `\"size\"`:
    integer\r\n- `\"start\"`: `{ \"x\": number, \"y\": number }`\r\n- `\"end\"`:
    `{ \"x\": number, \"y\": number }`\r\n- `\"tiles\"`: a flat array of objects
    with:\r\n  - `\"x\"`: column position\r\n  - `\"y\"`: row position\r\n  - `\"type\"`:
    integer 0\u20134\r\n  - `\"rotation\"`: 0, 90, 180, or 270\r\n\r\n\u26A0 Output
    only a single complete JSON object. Do not include markdown, explanation, or
    placeholder text like `{{x}}` or comment lines like // or /* */. The puzzle should
    NOT be already solved.\r\n\r\nNow generate a puzzle.\r\n"
